    {
      "block_id": "2605.23244_p4_b58",
      "text": "The proof of Theorem 4.1 is provided in Section A. Theo-\nrem 4.1 shows that LCOALA is convex. Thus, we can solve it\nto global optimality in polynomial time using more efficient\ngradient-based optimizers. Since we only have to train the\nweights of the final layer of the convex model, COALA re-\nquires significantly less computation than existing methods\nand provides the second major reason why COALA can\nquickly train on one GPU.\n",
      "bbox": [
        307.08,
        161.03,
        543.09,
        254.75
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        1228,
        644,
        2172,
