      "font_size": 9.96,
      "font_name": "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
      "is_math": false,
      "char_count": 64,
      "block_type": 0
    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.23244_p4_b66",
      "text": "CRONOS (Feng et al., 2024) is a specialized version of\nthe Alternating Direction Method of Multipliers (ADMM)\n(Boyd et al., 2011), for solving the optimization problem\nin (4). The choice of ADMM for solving (4) in Feng et al.\n(2024) is predicated on three key properties: (1) It possesses\na robust convergence guarantee as shown in Section 4.3, (2)\nit lifts memory constraints in LLM classification problems,\nand (3) it is highly optimized for GPU acceleration and\nparallelism in JAX.\n",
      "bbox": [
        307.11,
        593.86,
        543.19,
        699.54
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        1228,
